course: dictionary
lesson: 5887
title: Manta rays
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A manta is a very large, flat sea fish with wide fins like wings. Its full name is manta ray, and you can find it in warm oceans. «Manta rays are huge rays with wings up to about seven metres across.» The word huge tells you the fish is very big, and seven metres is longer than a car.
explain: Look at the clues in «Manta rays fly through the water on wings wider than a car is long.» The words fly, wings and through the water show that the fish glides through the sea the way a bird glides through the air. Ask yourself: what kind of creature could this be? A flat animal with wings that lives in water must be a sea creature.
explain: The word manta can also mean a blanket or cloak in Spanish-speaking countries, but this is rare in English. In a science lesson, manta always means the sea fish. Context tells you which meaning to use.
fact: A manta ray is a kind of ray, a flat fish with a wide body and wing-like fins.
fact: Manta rays can have wings up to about seven metres across.
fact: A manta ray eats tiny floating plankton by swimming with its mouth open.
fact: Manta rays are harmless to people, unlike stingrays.
fact: Manta rays have skeletons made of cartilage, not bone, and they are related to sharks.
exercise: «Manta rays are huge rays with wings up to about seven metres across.» What does huge mean here? | Very wet | *Very big | Very small | Very fast
exercise: «The manta ray is the biggest ray, with fins up to about 7 metres across.» What is a ray? | A type of bird | *A flat sea fish with wide fins | A kind of seaweed | A line of light in the sky
exercise: «It eats tiny floating plankton by swimming with its mouth open.» What does a manta ray eat? | Rubbish from boats | Fish from the rocks | Sea grass from the sea floor | *Tiny floating plankton
test: Are manta rays dangerous to people? | Only at night | Yes, they are very dangerous | Only in rivers | *No, they are harmless to people
test: In a science lesson, what does manta mean? | *A very large, flat sea fish | A type of whale | A soft blanket for a bed | A cloak from Spain
exam: Which clue in «Manta rays fly through the water on wings» best shows that a manta lives in the sea? | Wings | Fly | A blanket | *Through the water
